o as standalone forms. We will use the ControlContainer and @ViewChild decorators to achieve this.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3313e5f47faa4dcb41f930efcfdca63d","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2120-02-20T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"EHUz1Hbga","title":"How to use TS decorators to add caching logic to API calls","url":"https://indepth.dev/posts/1450/how-to-use-ts-decorators-to-add-caching-logic-to-api-calls","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-use-ts-decorators-to-add-caching-logic-to-api-calls-ehuz1hbga","summary":"Caching API calls reduces additional requests to the server-side, improves performance, and reduces data traffic. It's also possible to have more elaborate requirements like cache invalidation via an independent request to an external API service and emitting updated data to all subscribers. In this article I'll go over a couple of possible implementations that we considered.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a4f99f6561cd9ea7cb90bb20fd7b91e4","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2110-03-20T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"taSvdY7bt","title":"Angular in Depth","url":"https://angularindepth.com/posts/777/angular-in-depth-joins-forces-with-angular-love","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/angular-in-depth-tasvdy7bt","summary":"In-depth exploration of Angular, covering advanced features, performance optimization, and best practices for development.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/868c417ef79cfc270240bdaff12f8a88?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":22,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-09-12T08:03:13.979Z"},{"id":"SSL2OwhFN","title":"Angular in Depth","url":"https://angularindepth.com/posts/301/big-picture-operations","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/angular-in-depth-ssl2owhfn","summary":"Learn about the features and benefits of Angular, a popular JavaScript framework.","image":"https://media.da