ted_at":"2024-05-22T15:46:30.510Z"},{"id":"ruu40enBn","title":"Angular in Depth","url":"https://angularindepth.com/posts/1528/bundle-size-improvements-from-deferred-views-in-angular","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/angular-in-depth-ruu40enbn","summary":"Angular 17 introduces deferred views, allowing for fine-grained control over component loading to optimize app performance. By using dynamic imports and choosing triggers such as on idle, on viewport, on interaction, etc., developers can add components to the DOM as needed. Deferred views significantly reduce bundle size, improving download speed and optimizing app performance.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/df76d1c8005f122a8b877ac7cffe7c2c?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":8,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-03-11T14:37:39.755Z"},{"id":"HAWcK9wqr","title":"Angular in Depth","url":"https://angularindepth.com/posts/1527/strongly-typed-reactive-forms-in-angular","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/angular-in-depth-hawck9wqr","summary":"4 full days of Angular talks and workshops. Join in-person or virtually.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/df76d1c8005f122a8b877ac7cffe7c2c?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-03-11T14:37:39.734Z"}],"top_posts":[{"id":"tDLvaW3fg","title":"The Micro-Frontend Chaos (and how to solve it)","url":"https://indepth.dev/posts/1485/the-micro-frontend-chaos-and-how-to-solve-it","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-micro-frontend-chaos-and-how-to-solve-it--tdlvaw3fg","summary":"Micro-frontend allows us to use those different applications not just on the code base, but also in development, deployment and serve. Micro-frontends can load applications during run time without the need to build the entire dependency graph. But, even though, all of those applications are going to be hosted side by side as a single monolith on the user browser.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c249da29b82f5c23d5e9fb1e14fa6fab","num_upvotes":43,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-10-26T04:00:39.094Z"},{"id":"IS-w4BXXP","title":"101 Javascript Critical Rendering Path","url":"https://indepth.dev/posts/1498/101-javascript-critical-rendering-path","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/101-javascript-critical-rendering-path-is-w4bxxp","summary":"Every webpage has a Document Object Model or a DOM. This is an object-based representation of the entire HTML page, which is in the parsed state. Once the HTML is parsed, a DOM tree is built. The DOM Tree contains objects. The CSS Object Model takes care of the styles present in association with the DOM tree.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/2127e39c54896267599d7efcf3b696d2","num_upvotes":22,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2022-03-14T17:30:14.028Z"},{"id":"taSvdY7bt","title":"Angular in Depth","url":"https://angularindepth.com/posts/777/angular-in-depth-joins-forces-with-angular-love","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/angular-in-depth-tasvdy7bt","summary":"In-depth exploration of Angular, covering advanced features, performance optimization, and best practices for development.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/868c417ef79cfc270240bdaff12f8a88?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":22,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-09-12T08:03:13.979Z"},{"id":"7h2PDT7FR","title":"Exploring how virtual DOM is implemented in React","url":"https://indepth.dev/posts/1501/exploring-how-virtual-dom-is-implemented-in-react","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/exploring-how-virtual-dom-is-implemented-in-react-7h2pdt7fr","summary":"The virtual DOM is a tree-like structure that is used to represent a web page. It provides an interface through which developers can perform certain operations on that page, such as fetching information and altering the content/structure. It is the virtual DOM tha